      "writtenOn": "2019-05-09T00:38:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t look great. We are just trying to behave differently, wishing other devices don\u0027t do the same.\n\nI\u0027m questioning this holdoff timer now (including existing snk_ready_holdoff_timer). Are we really following the spec? Collision resolution is a part of the spec, isn\u0027t it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3372,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3376,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "8c7e3c949921b000d3274fa634d7072eb9c4c56a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cfa5ba8a_5d66dfe0",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3376,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-09T00:58:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For PD 2.0, I\u0027m not aware of any collision avoidance at the protocol level, whereas PD 3.0 has the SinkTxOk/NG scheme. Essentially, the source adjusts the Rp to signal an atomic message sequence.\n\nThere\u0027s probably some collision avoidance when actually transmitting the messages at the PHY level for PD 2.0.\n\nAs for the hold off timer, I don\u0027t think we\u0027re breaking the spec. Once you\u0027ve established a contract, I\u0027m not aware of any required timing for future messages. For example, a DiscIdent message must be responded to, but I\u0027m not aware of any timing as to when it must be sent. Another example would be a PR swap which can happen at any time.\n\nBut, you\u0027re totally right. We\u0027re just hoping we don\u0027t collide by waiting a bit. It\u0027s entirely possible for another partner to wait this same time and we\u0027d just end up colliding with them.",
      "parentUuid": "6bf3f12b_efb198e2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3372,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3376,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "8c7e3c949921b000d3274fa634d7072eb9c4c56a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5746ee08_1f728fbb",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3376,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-09T01:29:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This holdoff timer may just create new collision(s) which are currently working. So, I\u0027m not sure we\u0027re improving compatibility or decreasing it. \n\nWe should seek for a solution which avoids or resolves any collision (instead of fixing one particular collision) until we know this is a limitation for PD 2.0.",
      "parentUuid": "cfa5ba8a_5d66dfe0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3372,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3376,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "8c7e3c949921b000d3274fa634d7072eb9c4c56a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a805a605_f30dfe66",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3376,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-09T17:28:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For an idea, should we track the last timestamp of the last received packet and wait to send our packets after a certain quiet time has elapsed (or a maximum wait time).\n\nWe could wait for 50ms +- 10ms (+- depending on wall clock for randomness or something like that) after the last received packet to send our data\n\nThoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "5746ee08_1f728fbb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3372,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3376,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "8c7e3c949921b000d3274fa634d7072eb9c4c56a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1da08dd8_c0ab205b",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3376,
